            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> mini.git data buffer `<head_name>` is missing if there is no commit in the git repo.\n> \n> it's understandable that `<head>` since there in no commit, but imo the branch name should be available.\n\nThis works as expected: there is no `head_name` since there is no (valid) `HEAD`. Executing `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` shows an `ambiguous argument 'HEAD': unknown revision or path not in the working tree` error.\n\nTechnically speaking, there is no branches yet either: `git branch -a` shows nothing.\n\nSo I'd say this works as expected.",
